# SRG-APP-000175-WSR-000095  -  CAT II
# The web server must perform RFC 5280-compliant certification path
# validation.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000175-WSR-000095
group:           V-206388
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000185
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Certification path validation for the Splunk Web channel is driven by the
                 same two splunkd settings: the certificate authority store that supplies
                 the trust anchor, and the certificate status validation method that adds
                 revocation status to the path check.

governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           server.conf [sslConfig] certificateStatusValidationMethod equals crl
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] certificateStatusValidationMethod https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The path validation algorithm itself is implemented by the cryptographic
                 library shipped with the product; its RFC 5280 conformance is a property
                 of that library, not a configurable setting
external:        CRL files must be present and current in the instance's auth/crl
                 directory, supplied by the issuing certificate authority
external:        Not Applicable where the web server does not use PKI

citation:        SRG-APP-000175-WSR-000095 check text (RFC 5280-compliant path validation;
                 Not Applicable where PKI is not used); server.conf.spec:1125-1147
                 (certificateStatusValidationMethod = crl is the only acceptable value,
                 default empty string turns the checks off, and the checks apply to the
                 Splunk Web channel as well), server.conf.spec:996-1010 (sslRootCAPath, no
                 default), web.conf.spec:108-119 (web.conf sslRootCAPath is used only when
                 requireClientCert and enableCertBasedUserAuth are both true and otherwise
                 falls back to server.conf)
finding:         server.conf [sslConfig] does not set certificateStatusValidationMethod =
                 crl or leaves sslRootCAPath empty, so the Splunk Web channel does not
                 perform path validation to a named trust anchor with revocation status.
